  "handoff": {
    "summary": "The rows-plus-flat-list matrix constructor now reuses an exact built-in list during dimension inference instead of copying it before MatrixSpace performs its owned FLINT import. Matrix ownership remains independent of the source list, while list subclasses and general iterables retain observable iteration semantics. The public benchmark now compares rows-only construction with the established explicit-shape no-copy form: warm 500x500 medians were 16.92 ms and 14.31 ms in the recorded run. A separate interleaved diagnostic measured the removed copy directly at 16.90 ms versus 8.61 ms for 500x500 and 70.29 ms versus 40.19 ms for 1000x1000. Integration rebuilt the combined self-hosted tree and passed focused semantics, strict baselib, architecture, and the complete 117-test portable tier.",
    "risks": [
      "Absolute microbenchmark times remain sensitive to host contention, so the benchmark combines generous absolute ceilings with a rows-only versus explicit-shape parity check."
    ],
    "next_steps": []
  }
